                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "L1Kwz",
              "name": "Sanskrit Verse",
              "fill": "$ash",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "मातृदेवो भव । पितृदेवो भव ।\nआचार्यदेवो भव । अतिथिदेवो भव ।\nयान्यनवद्यानि कर्माणि तानि सेवितव्यानि । नो इतराणि ।",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "textAlign": "center",
              "fontFamily": "$font-deva",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "NtlhZ",
              "name": "Translation",
              "fill": "$ash-muted",
              "content": "Treat your mother as a god. Treat your father as a god.\nTreat your teacher as a god. Treat your guest as a god.\nWhatever deeds are blameless, those you should follow.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "textAlign": "center",
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "fontStyle": "italic"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "x87sb",
              "name": "Not the others",
              "fill": "$kumkum",
              "content": "Not the others.",
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 19,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "fontStyle": "italic"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "YKVyC",
              "name": "Citation",
              "fill": "$ash-muted",
              "content": "TAITTIRIYA UPANISHAD  1.11.2",
              "fontFamily": "$font-label",
              "fontSize": 9,
              "fontWeight": "500",
              "letterSpacing": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Qy2oZ",
          "name": "Blurb",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "P1dq42",
              "name": "Paragraph 1",
              "fill": "$ash",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "On Moti Fali, in the village of Pal Gam in Surat, nobody used his real name. The street called him Shambu, one of Shiva's own names. Honest. Devout. The man the Samaj sent for first, for every wedding and every funeral.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ugWhK",
              "name": "Paragraph 2",
              "fill": "$kumkum",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "His family knew a different man.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "fontStyle": "italic"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "XWLtx",
              "name": "Paragraph 3",
              "fill": "$ash",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "In this true story, his son tells what happened behind the door the street never saw. A grandfather tied to his bed and beaten for his drinking. A mother who cooked for nine, paid the household's bills, and was hit for disagreeing. Two children who grew up afraid of their own father. And a son whose own marriage was decided by one question: what will the Samaj say?",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "O998Y",
              "name": "Paragraph 4",
              "fill": "$ash",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Ferin Patel holds his father up against the scriptures he took such pride in knowing. The result is a son's reckoning, and a mirror for every family still living behind a respectable front door.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "a5Pbw",
          "name": "Footer",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "gap": 24,
          "justifyContent": "space_between",
          "alignItems": "end",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Q5XFb4",
              "name": "Author Bio",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "rectangle",
                  "id": "BS88k",
                  "name": "Rule",
                  "fill": "$kumkum",
                  "width": 28,
                  "height": 2
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "WOwkN",
                  "name": "Bio",
                  "fill": "$ash-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Ferin Patel grew up on Moti Fali in Surat, Gujarat. He now lives in Halifax, Canada, where he works in software.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
